# The five assets under public/home/** that the storefront actually renders are
# kept OUT of LFS: Vercel's checkout does not fetch LFS objects, so anything in
# LFS deploys as its ~132-byte pointer file — the hero video and the banner
# stills were being served as text with a video/png content type, which is why
# nothing played or painted in production. Later rules win, so these override
# the public/home/** line above. Everything else in that folder (730MB of films
# the site no longer references) stays in LFS.
public/home/hero/*.png !filter !diff !merge -text
public/home/real-projects/virtual-showroom-tour.mp4 !filter !diff !merge -text
